{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/480860-coyote-falls-sas-is-it-any-good","id":480860,"title":"Coyote Falls SAS: Is it any good?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T16:35:42-07:00","id":480860,"title":"Coyote Falls SAS: Is it any good?","content":"Hi! As I've already said in the title, I'm looking particularly for actual play experience. I'm reading it right now, but I was looking for some extra practical advice.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T16:59:03-07:00","id":481726,"title":"","content":"I ran it as the first part of my first chronicle. It's quite well done with a lot of space to expand or change things (like setting, I switched mine to rural Canada). I'd recommend switching it over to 2e Werewolf: the Forsaken, which shouldn't be hard. I also didn't use the pregen characters, my group created their own.<br /> <br /> All in all I think it does a very solid job of introducing players to Werewolf, the themes of spirit and flesh in a well recognized setting in Colorado, which has been expanded upon in various books. My players thoroughly enjoyed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Membe